अ॑थ adv. then, now;
 therefore, accordingly;
 further,
also;
 however, but (often merely expletive). At the beginning of books
or sections of books = now beginneth (opp. इति q.v.). Often followed
by अतस् (अथातस्), अपि (अथापि), उ (अथो), घ, तु, पुनर्, etc. —
अथ वा (r. अथ alone or वाथ) or, or rather, but, however, or
if, even. अथ वा—अथ वा either or. अथ किम् how else?, i.e. of
course. अथ किमु so much the more.

